<title>GERMANY: Duesseldorf air cargo rises 85.7pct in April 97.</title>
<headline>Duesseldorf air cargo rises 85.7pct in April 97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total flown air cargo handled at Duesseldorf airport (DUS) soared 85.7pct in April to 5,609 tonnes, figures from the German airports association ADV showed.</p>
<p>Air cargo growth over the first four months of 1997 at Duesseldorf was 33.3 percent, the monthly ADV traffic report said.</p>
<p>But the high April growth is a statistical blip since the April 11, 1996, fire disaster at Duesseldorf forced all air cargo to be switched to other airports and provoked an artificial slump, observers noted.</p>
<p>The following tables show cargo handled at Duesseldorf airport in April and for the year to date in tonnes and with year-on-year percentage changes.</p>
<p>    April 1997		    Monthly total	Pct change</p>
<p>    Total flown cargo		5,609		Up   85.7</p>
<p>    Exports			    2,846		Up   93.7</p>
<p>    Imports			    2,632		Up   79.3</p>
<p>    Transit				131		     n/a</p>
<p>    Jan-April 1997	     Cumulative total    Pct change</p>
<p>    Total flown cargo	     22,271		Up   33.3</p>
<p>    Exports			   10,339		Up   37.2</p>
<p>    Imports			   11,389		Up   31.3</p>
<p>    Transit				543		     n/a</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research dept.</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
